.TH FLEET-DB 1 "2026-10-12" "cti-agent 1.3" "CTI Fleet Manual"
.SH NAME
fleet-db \- the fleet's SQLite memory: findings, digests sent, tasks, notes and board mail
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fleet\-db init
.br
.B fleet\-db remember
.I category topic content...
.br
.B fleet\-db recent
.RI [ n ]
.br
.B fleet\-db task add
.I title...
.br
.B fleet\-db task done
.I id
.br
.B fleet\-db task list
.br
.B fleet\-db mail send
.I agent kind body...
.br
.B fleet\-db mail inbox
.I agent
.br
.B fleet\-db mail ack
.I id
.br
.B fleet\-db ack
.I id
.br
.B fleet\-db finding
.RI [ word " [" json... ]]
.br
.B fleet\-db findings
.RB [ \-\-priority
.IR BAND ]
.RB [ \-\-stale\-days
.IR N ]
.br
.B fleet\-db rollup
.RB [ \-\-days
.IR N ]
.br
.B fleet\-db note
.I cve
.RI [ text... ]
.br
.B fleet\-db sent
.I day s5 s4 s3 s2 s1 message_id
.RI [ kind ]
.br
.B fleet\-db was\-sent
.I day
.RI [ kind ]
.br
.B fleet\-db vacuum
.PP
.B sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db
.I command
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fleet\-db
is the only writer of
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/memory.db ,
the database that holds what the fleet has concluded and what it has done.
It is called by the runners
.RB ( run\-digest (1)
records each send with
.B sent
and checks
.B was\-sent
before sending again; the weekly digest is built from
.BR rollup ),
by
.B enrich.py
(which upserts every enriched finding through
.BR finding ),
by
.B cti\-jira
.RB ( note ),
and by the orchestrator heartbeat, whose tool allowlist grants only
.BR recent ,
.BR findings ,
.BR was\-sent ,
.BR rollup ,
.BR remember ,
.BR task ,
.BR mail ,
.B ack
and
.BR vacuum .
.PP
Every invocation except a bare
.B fleet\-db
creates any missing table and index, then applies the severity migration:
.B digests
columns
.BR p1 .. p4
become
.BR sev5 .. sev1
(the new Sev3 column starts at 0), and stored
.B findings.priority
values P1, P2, P3, P4 are rewritten to Sev5, Sev4, Sev2, Sev1. Each step is
guarded, so it runs once and costs one
.B PRAGMA
thereafter; what it changed is reported on standard error. The database is
opened in WAL mode with a 5-second busy timeout so lanes can read while one
writes.
.PP
Arguments are positional and not validated beyond what the code needs: a
missing argument, or a non-number where an id or count is expected, ends in
a Python traceback and exit status 1. Text arguments after the fixed ones
are joined with single spaces, so quoting is optional.
.PP
.B fleet\-db
sends no mail and makes no network calls.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B init
Create the schema and run the migration, then print
.BI "initialized " path\fR.
Idempotent.
.B install.sh
runs it once; on the Fedora layout the schema is created by the first
command that touches the database, since every command does the same.
.TP
.BI remember " category topic content..."
Store a free-text memory with the current UTC time. Prints
.BR ok .
.TP
.BR recent " [\fIn\fR]"
Print the
.I n
newest memories (default 20, each truncated to 160 characters), every open
task, every unacknowledged mailbox message (body truncated to 120
characters), and a count of findings per priority band
.RB ( unscored
for rows with none). The orchestrator reads this at the start of each beat.
.TP
.BI "task add" " title..."
Add an open task.
.TP
.BI "task done" " id"
Mark task
.I id
done and record when.
.TP
.B task list
Every task, open ones first, as
.B [ ]
or
.BR [x] .
.IP
Any other word after
.B task
does nothing and exits 0.
.TP
.BI "mail send" " agent kind body..."
Queue a message for
.I agent
(a board handle such as
.BR @enrich ).
.TP
.BI "mail inbox" " agent"
Unacknowledged messages for
.IR agent ,
oldest first.
.TP
.BI "mail ack" " id"
.TQ
.BI ack " id"
Mark message
.I id
acknowledged. The two forms are identical.
.IP
Any other word after
.B mail
does nothing and exits 0.
.TP
.BR finding " [\fIword\fR [\fIjson...\fR]]"
Insert or update findings, keyed on
.BR cve .
The JSON, a single object or an array of objects, is taken from the
arguments after the first (the first is ignored; callers write
.BR upsert ),
or from standard input when there are none. Recognised keys are
.BR cve ,
.BR status ,
.BR provider ,
.BR qids ,
.BR host_count ,
.BR qualys_score ,
.BR last_seen ,
.BR sample_hosts ,
.BR cvss ,
.BR cvss_severity ,
.BR epss ,
.BR epss_pct ,
.BR kev ,
.BR kev_added ,
.BR kev_due ,
.BR ransomware ,
.BR priority ,
.B rationale
and
.BR description ;
others are ignored. On an existing row every recognised column is replaced
(a key absent from the JSON becomes NULL) and
.B updated
is set to now;
.B first_seen
is set only when the row is created, and
.B remediation_note
is never touched. Prints
.BI "upserted " N " findings"\fR.
Not on the heartbeat's allowlist: it rewrites what the digest reports.
.TP
.BR findings " [\fB\-\-priority\fR \fIBAND\fR] [\fB\-\-stale\-days\fR \fIN\fR]"
Print stored findings as a JSON array, ordered by priority then host count,
largest first.
.B \-\-priority
keeps one band, written exactly as stored
.RB ( Sev5 ,
.BR Sev4 ,
.BR Sev3 ,
.BR Sev2 ,
.BR Sev1 ).
.B \-\-stale\-days
.I N
keeps only findings with no remediation note whose
.B updated
time is more than
.I N
days ago; timestamps are compared as datetimes, so a row from the cutoff's
own calendar day is counted correctly. Both may be given.
.TP
.BR rollup " [\fB\-\-days\fR \fIN\fR]"
Print, on standard output, a JSON document in the shape
.B enrich.py
writes, built from stored findings rather than from a mailbox read: every
finding updated or first seen in the last
.I N
days (default 7), each with
.B is_new
set when
.B first_seen
falls inside the window. It carries all five band counts even when zero
(plus
.B unscored
when a row has no priority),
.BR total ,
an empty
.BR degraded ,
.B kev_deadlines
with
.B overdue
and
.B worst_overdue_days
counted over every row with a
.B kev_due
date, and a
.B source_meta.rollup
line saying no mailbox was read. It has no
.B email_subjects
key, so the digest omits its emails section.
.B run\-digest weekly
renders this with
.BR brief.py (1).
.TP
.BR note " \fIcve\fR [\fItext...\fR]"
Set the finding's
.B remediation_note
(who is handling it, a ticket key) and its
.B updated
time. With no
.I text
the note is cleared. A finding with a note is no longer reported by
.BR "findings \-\-stale\-days" .
A CVE with no row prints
.BI "no finding for " cve " \- note not recorded"
and still exits 0, because a ticket can exist for a CVE the table has not
seen.
.TP
.BR sent " \fIday s5 s4 s3 s2 s1 message_id\fR [\fIkind\fR]"
Record that the
.I kind
digest
.RB ( daily
by default;
.B weekly
for the weekly) went out for
.I day
.RB ( YYYY\-MM\-DD ),
with the five band counts as integers and the Graph request id. A second
record for the same kind and day replaces the first. Prints
.BR logged .
Not on the heartbeat's allowlist: a fake record makes
.B run\-digest
skip that day's real send.
.TP
.BR was\-sent " \fIday\fR [\fIkind\fR]"
Print
.B yes
and exit 0 if a
.I kind
digest (default
.BR daily )
is recorded for
.IR day ;
otherwise print
.B no
and exit 1.
.TP
.B vacuum
Compact the database. Prints
.BR vacuumed .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B fleet\-db
does not read
.I fleet.env
itself.
.TP
.B FLEET_HOME
State directory; the database is
.IR $FLEET_HOME/state/memory.db ,
and
.I $FLEET_HOME/state
is created if missing.
Default:\~\fI~/fleet\fR. Set to
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent
by the systemd units and
.BR cti\-agent (1)
(\fIfleet.env\fR section 3, PATHS, records the same value).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/cti\-agent/state/memory.db
The database, with its
.I \-wal
and
.I \-shm
companions. Tables:
.BR memories ,
.BR tasks ,
.BR mailbox ,
.BR findings ,
.B scout_items
(written by
.BR scout.py ),
.BR digests .
.TP
.I /opt/cti\-agent/bin/fleet\-db
The program.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command ran, including
.B note
for an unknown CVE, an unrecognised
.B task
or
.B mail
sub-command, and a
.B findings
query that matched nothing.
.TP
.B 1
.B was\-sent
found no record; or a missing or malformed argument, invalid JSON for
.BR finding ,
or a database error (Python traceback on standard error).
.TP
.B 2
No command, or an unknown one; the usage text is printed. An unknown
command still creates the schema and runs the migration first.
.SH EXAMPLES
What the fleet remembers, and the band counts:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db recent 40
.EE
.PP
Exploited and present, and anything nobody has picked up in a week:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db findings \-\-priority Sev5
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db findings \-\-stale\-days 7
.EE
.PP
Record who is handling a finding, then clear it again:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db note CVE\-2026\-1234 SEC\-101 host\-a team
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db note CVE\-2026\-1234
.EE
.PP
Did today's daily go out? Preview the weekly's input:
.PP
.EX
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db was\-sent $(date +%F) daily
sudo cti\-agent fleet\-db rollup \-\-days 7 | less
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fleet\-board (1),
.BR enrich.py (1),
.BR scout.py (1),
.BR brief.py (1),
.BR run\-digest (1),
.BR cti\-agent (1),
.BR sqlite3 (1)
.PP
RUNBOOK.md section 12; fleet\-kit/fleet/CLAUDE.md, "Message board".
